A||||14||loafer87gt||Got a 72 VW van!||||7||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||07-30-2001||12:52 AM||||I just made a deal with my Dad to trade my 87GT with the bad engine (bearing shot) for a 72 VW van! The body is pretty bad, but the engine has just been rebuilt and the interior is in perfect condition. Being an artsy hippy type feller, I can see myself getting quite attached to it. The good thing about trading my car to my pop is that he is absolutely obsessed with his vehicles, so he'll fix every little problem with my GT, so when I'm done school I can buy the car back from him and have it like new again. I was surprised when I checked JC Whitney by how much aftermarket stuff there is for it. I found a set of headers and dual exhaust for 189 US! I think first on the to do list is to replace the lower body panels and get a electric heater conversion. I can't wait till the first day of college to start now to show off the new wheels||||reg||7
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-30-2001||01:30 AM||||Peace, Moonbeam.....make love, not war.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||07-30-2001||02:25 AM||||Just stick a 500 caddy in the back.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">Hopefully attached to some sort of transaxle and not just there for extra weight though you might be able to pull wheelies either way.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||07-30-2001||06:27 AM||||"Pull wheelies"?  In a '72 VW van?  Get real.  Early air cooled VWs were about the only vehicle with less hp than a Yugo.<P>Nice acquisition, though.  I always thought the VW vans were kinda neat, although I'm not much of the hippie type.  Which model did you get?  Camper, cargo or passenger?  The camper versions (did they call them Westfalias back then?) were pretty practical for the time.  I always thought the pop up roof was cool.  Now I'm rambling.  Post some pics.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||07-30-2001||07:41 AM|||| I Love VW Vans. I have a 77 Westfalia camper. Engine needs a rebuild, but it,s one fine vehicle. Most practical camper ever made.<BR> Two double beds. sink , stove, refridge, 2 liter, AC, 90 hp. It will run 90 mph all day if asked. Older vans were as little as 36 hp.||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||07-30-2001||02:04 PM||||It's a passenger model. Cream colored with a big Canadian maple leaf on the front. It was the first vehicle I ever drove when I was a kid, and we even made a four day treck up to the Northwest territories in it before we parked it. It'll be perfect for carting around my huge art canvas', not to mention how many people I'll be able to pack in for the drive in. I'll get some pics next time I swing home, like I said the body is pretty rough, but the interior is primo and it has a lot of character.||||reg||6
