Z||000013||beer_stud_21||08-02-2001||05:34 AM||||Some of my earliest vehicular memories are of our VW van "kermit"  It was a dark green and white split window VW passenger van.  When I was like 5 My mom and I drove from Pt Townsend Wa, to Northern Cali.  I had the job of holding the thing in gear!  hehe.  I also remember it had no power what so ever and would over heat a lot.  That van also permanently instilled the seat belt rule in my brain.  My dad demonstrated why I should wear my seatbelt one day when I refused to put mine on.  Slammed on the brakes going like 10 miles an hour. I flew off that back seat right into that sheet metal that held up the front passenger seat.  I'm sure I got a fat lip from that one.  Will never forget it tho.  Will probably save my ass one of these days!<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000014||mblackwell||08-03-2001||05:15 AM||||There is a website somwhere about a guy who put an air-cooled Porsche engine in one of those.  It had pics of it doing wheelies.||||reg||1
